# ── Env files — NEVER commit real credentials ─────────────────────────────────
# .env, .env.local, .env.production, .env.development.local etc. all contain
# real secrets (database passwords, API keys, JWT secrets) and must NEVER be
# committed or pushed to any repository, public or private.
.env
.env.*
.env*
# Exception: .env.example is safe to commit — it contains only placeholders.
!.env.example

